# Deny everything, then allow back exactly what the build needs.
#
# An allowlist rather than a denylist because the build context is otherwise
# ~700 MB of things the image must never see (.git 145 MB, .venv 501 MB, plus
# caches and notebooks), and because a denylist grows a hole every time someone
# adds a directory.
#
# CAREFUL: pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"` and
# `license = {file = "LICENSE"}`, so hatchling reads both at build time. Dropping
# either from this allowlist does not fail as a missing COPY — it fails deeper,
# inside `pip install .`.
*

!titiler
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
